### 1. Valid booking (expect 201)
POST http://localhost:3000/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": 1,
  "customerName": "Sam",
  "customerEmail": "sam@example.com",
  "startsAt": "2026-12-01T15:00:00.000Z"
}

### 2. Same slot again (expect 409)
POST http://localhost:3000/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": 1,
  "customerName": "Alex",
  "customerEmail": "alex@example.com",
  "startsAt": "2026-12-01T15:00:00.000Z"
}

### 3. Overlaps the first booking (expect 409)
POST http://localhost:3000/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": 2,
  "customerName": "Alex",
  "customerEmail": "alex@example.com",
  "startsAt": "2026-12-01T15:30:00.000Z"
}

### 4. In the past (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:3000/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": 1,
  "customerName": "Sam",
  "customerEmail": "sam@example.com",
  "startsAt": "2020-01-01T10:00:00.000Z"
}

### 5. Service that doesn't exist (expect 404)
POST http://localhost:3000/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": 99,
  "customerName": "Sam",
  "customerEmail": "sam@example.com",
  "startsAt": "2026-12-05T10:00:00.000Z"
}

### 6. List Sam's bookings (expect 200)
GET http://localhost:3000/bookings?email=sam@example.com